A||||13||johnt671||Results of Steering Damper Removal||||10||
Z||000000||johnt671||11-23-2001||02:41 PM||||Just took mine off and went for a ride on some twisty back roads.  Liked the feeling and didn't notice a jerky steering wheel.  Steering was lighter and I can feel the tires react to changes to steering input.  Next tests will be a rougher road and the highway.||||reg||10
Z||000001||StuGood||11-23-2001||03:33 PM||||Now that's what I call undamped enthusiasm...||||reg||12
Z||000002||maryjane||11-23-2001||04:18 PM||||It was my experience that you don't notice any thing bad till you are on rough roads, making steering corrections. Some people never notice anything different tho. guess it depends on the driver & the car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||11-23-2001||05:35 PM||||first thing to go on my Fiero and Mercedes SL. I liked quicker response better than sluggish feel with them.||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnt671||11-23-2001||07:26 PM||||It passed the rough road test.  Took it down one before and it was ok.  Last test will be the highway test in the A.M.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||11-23-2001||07:45 PM||||Find some rain grooves, or find a place where they've roughed up the pavement in order to apply a new topcoat.<BR>My 85 GT (Bought new. Sold with 24,000 miles.) used to fight me on roads like that.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||MrPBody||11-23-2001||09:02 PM||||Next step -- if you have 14" Hi-Tech alloy wheels -- install '80's Grand Am wheels on the front.  They look identical but are offset more to the inside; they will further lighten your steering and reduce kickback.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||johnt671||11-24-2001||08:01 AM||||I've got aftermarket 5 spokes on it.  Not sure of the offset but told the guy I wanted a close to stock offset so the car didn't look like Mickey Mouse going down the road.||||reg||1
Z||000008||conductor||11-24-2001||08:32 AM||||These 14 inch Hi-techs,what do they look like?<BR>Has anyone a picture?<BR>Grtx Richard||||reg||1
Z||000009||longjonsilver||11-24-2001||08:51 AM||||i took off my steering damper over 17 years ago - 84 2m4 - bot new dec 10th 1983 - and would not put it on - except to pass safety whatevers - the handling improved in all conditions - even the BUMPY road thru my vineyard - although it cracked the windshield! my steering was not adversly affected.<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by johnt671:<BR><B>Just took mine off and went for a ride on some twisty back roads.  Liked the feeling and didn't notice a jerky steering wheel.  Steering was lighter and I can feel the tires react to changes to steering input.  Next tests will be a rougher road and the highway.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>au revoir||||reg||6
Z||000010||johnt671||11-24-2001||11:32 AM||||Just took it on the highway.  Done good.  I ddidn't feel any of the downsides mentioned.  It also made the steering lighter in parking lots which was what I had hoped for due to a sometimes stiff back.  A ten minute mod that that seems to have had no downside.  Now if only horsepower was as easy.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fieroman_5000||11-24-2001||11:54 AM||||how do you remove the steering dampner (*spelling?) anywayz? 'caue i want to do it!!<P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||johnt671||11-24-2001||01:07 PM||||It's like a small shock absorber.  I just parked the car on a small hill, slid under the car sprayed it don and took it off.  There are only two bolts holding the damper on, take them off and pull the damper off and you're done.  Not even a 5 minute job.||||reg||1
Z||000013||MrPBody||11-24-2001||01:13 PM||||conductor --<P>I'm referring to stock 14" aluminum wheels like those on <A HREF="http://home.att.net/~cochrans/fiero_01.htm" TARGET=_blank>my car</A>.<BR>||||reg||1
